  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/58627d2c-c12b-4a75-b01e-123bacc31b00.png\" style=\"width: 374px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p><math><mi>P</mi></math> is one of the end points of the latus rectum.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math><mi>Q</mi></math> lies on the directrix.<br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />Equation of the normal at <math><mi>R</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
